## Derivation Methodology (layered evidence stack)

1. **Competitive desk research** — Klaviyo/Mailchimp/Shopify/emerging-threat product pages, help center, pricing, case studies; third-party comparisons (Costbench, Jellyreach, AI:Productivity, Nudgify, Omnisend, etc.)
2. **Public VoC** — Qualitative synthesis (NOT statistical NLP): G2, Trustpilot, Capterra, Reddit, vendor communities, agency blogs, YouTube. Thematic coding into Love/Hate/Mixed + net-sentiment scores (qualitative, not computed)
3. **Slack HVC VoC** (Mailchimp internal) — `#hvc_feedback`, `#mc-hvc-escalations`, `#mc-feedback-summary`; HVC = $299+/mo MRR; dedup by user+quote; keyword + negative sentiment filter
4. **HeyMarvin UX research** — 50 videos → Whisper → 21 customer briefs → synthesis; repo: github.com/deepakp1308/mailchimp-automation-research (Intuit-internal)
5. **BigQuery product health** — `bi_aggregate.product_journey_monthly` (89.4M rows), `mbr_monthly`; stages Unexplored→Explore→Try→Establish→Abandon
6. **PRD audit** — 9 Elizabeth Bertasi PDFs mapped to evidence gaps
7. **Repo forensics** — CJB (`crmmktg-mktauto`) and NUNI (`collab-email`) GitHub org analysis
8. **Cross-tab synthesis** — Initiative Canvas (72 initiatives), Strategy 6-Pager, Growth Model, Loss Attribution

## Cross-Competitor Gap Mappings (in mailchimp.html Initiative Canvas)

- **Klaviyo: 26 named gaps** — 5-channel canvas, Marketing Agent, Flows AI, predictive triggers, Smart Send Time, Channel Affinity, Universal Content, free-tier flows, etc. → P2/P4/P5 initiatives
- **Shopify: 16 named gaps** — Sidekick conversational editing (D1 headline steal), native commerce data, free bundling, Flow ops scale → P4/P5
- **Emerging threats: 6 companies** — vertical slices (Customer.io SaaS, Postscript Shopify SMS, Auxia agentic, etc.)

## Key Strategic Numbers (Mailchimp Automations FY27)

- **Target:** +$20–25M automation ARR (lower band of $20–32M envelope)
- **HVC exposure:** $177.5K/mo (73 themes, automation); $70K/mo nav/search (separate)
- **Product health:** CJB Established 132K (+18.4% YoY); Activation 33.6%; Churn 40.2%; Free CJB adoption 1.1%
- **Binding constraint:** Activation funnel, not capability (customers use 10–20% of features)
- **Critical dependency:** Eventbus migration gates P3–P5 (real-time triggers, WhatsApp, conversational)

## Competitive Positioning Summary

- **Klaviyo:** DTC depth moat (Shopify gravity, 5-channel canvas, 10+ in-flow AI, Marketing Agent); exposed on pricing (Feb 2025 active-profile model), support, UI redesign backlash
- **Shopify:** Free/default starter ("good enough, often free"); exposed on channel depth, A/B testing, predictive triggers; hybrid pattern "Klaviyo flows + Shopify Email broadcast"
- **Mailchimp:** Strong UX simplicity + brand; squeezed from below (Shopify free) and above (Klaviyo depth); Classic deprecation June 2025 gutted free tier
- **Emerging:** Death by verticalized cuts (4.65/5 G2 avg); no single replacement

## Unified Builder FY27 (Editor lane, separate from CJB)

- **4 pillars:** P1 Trust, P2 Universal Content/Migration, P3 AI/TTV, P4 Omni-channel
- **~$21M ARR target;** critical path: rendering parity → Universal Content → AI Setup Agent → shared email+SMS blocks → co-editing
- **Freddie concern:** 0/17 HVC themes solved; AI shipping 8× faster than trust fixes

